Qui nous sommes ?

Artefact est une nouvelle génération de cabinet de conseil spécialisée en Data &amp; IA, de la stratégie, au déploiement, jusqu’à l’adoption.&nbsp;

Artefact c’est aussi&nbsp; 2500 employés répartis sur 26 pays ont pour mission d’accompagner la transformation chez nos clients.

Nous offrons une large gamme de solutions Data et IA driven, que nous adaptions aux besoins spécifiques de nos clients, que ce soit des projets IA pour l'automatisation des process internes à chaque étape de leur chaîne de valeur, la création d'expériences consommateurs innovantes et personnalisées, le conseil en stratégie data et marketing digital jusqu'à la gestion du mix-média et plus encore !

La performance de nos services data repose sur une réelle expertise technologique en Intelligence Artificielle et des compétences métiers acquises auprès de plus de 1000 clients dans le monde, tels que Legrand, AccorHotels, Orange, Carrefour, Engie, Emirates, Deutsche Telekom, Carrefour, etc.

La force d'Artefact repose sur un mix unique d'atouts: une connaissance des technologies de pointe en Data et IA, des méthodes agiles permettant de délivrer très rapidement les projets et des équipes composées des meilleurs experts dans leurs domaines (strategy et business consultants, analytics engineers, data scientists, data engineers, UX/UI, etc.).

Practice : AI Strategy &amp; Transformation&nbsp;

Contexte
Nous renforçons notre practice AI Strategy &amp; Transformation avec un(e) Partner chargé(e) d'accompagner nos clients grands comptes, tous secteurs confondus, dans la définition et l'exécution de leurs stratégies IA.&nbsp;

Company Overview

Metrea delivers effects-as-a-service to national security partners across five domains and more than a dozen mission areas. These include airborne ISR, electronic warfare, secure communications, aerial refueling, special air missions, aerial firefighting, and advanced simulation. We own the whole stack: designing, building, and operating turnkey capabilities that give our partners decisive, asymmetric advantage against rapidly evolving threats.

Our operating model is built around three interlocking pillars. The Support Groups provide a global shared-service - spanning people, finance, platform, operations, legal, and engagement. This frees up our Core Groups, who develop and own mission capabilities end-to-end, to focus entirely on delivery. The Market Groups apply a regional lens, ensuring that our agile and adaptable capabilities remain aligned to the wicked problems that matter most to our partners across the Americas, EMEA, and Asia-Pacific.

At the heart of our model is a simple but powerful idea: be a true partner with skin in the game. Our partners need effects, not just equipment. By owning the full stack - from the lab to the field - we are able to drive a continuous cycle of innovation that keeps our partners ahead. It's a fast-moving, intellectually demanding environment where talented people are given real responsibility, work on problems that matter, and contribute to an enterprise that is growing quickly and deliberately.

Headquartered in Washington, DC, with facilities across the United States, the United Kingdom, as well as Continental Europe and Asia-Pacific.

Position Summary

In this role, you will directly enable operational and mission readiness by ensuring critical aviation parts, equipment, and materials are available where and when they are needed-often in remote or austere environments. As a Material Handler, you are a trusted operator responsible for the accuracy, movement, and accountability of high-value, compliance-sensitive materials supporting global operations. &nbsp;

You will be successful if you can execute&nbsp; logistics &nbsp;with speed, discipline, and precision while navigating export controls, 3PL&nbsp; (third-party&nbsp; logistics )&nbsp; warehouse relations, aviation regulations, and complex supply chains. Your effectiveness is measured by&nbsp; aircraft availability, operational continuity, and the confidence others place in your judgement. &nbsp;

Initially, you will help establish Metrea’s regional aviation materials and logistics capability in Munich, creating the processes and infrastructure needed to support European operations. You will often operate as the sole logistics specialist onsite, taking hands-on ownership of the complete materials lifecycle while working closely with aircraft maintainers, flight crews and site leaders. &nbsp;

What You'll Do

• Help establish and continuously improve Metrea’s European regional aviation materials and logistics capability. &nbsp;

• Receive purchase orders, process inbound shipments, and coordinate domestic and international shipments to meet operational requirements

• Manage aviation inventory including stocking, put-away, inventory control, material tracking, and parts issuance

• Manage the complete material lifecycle, including receiving, inspection, system entry, storage, stock control, parts issuance, returns, repair movements and reverse logistics . &nbsp;

• Create and receive orders within our ERP/WMS platforms and prepare commercial invoices and other international shipping documentation. &nbsp;

• Prioriti s e and process parts requests based on operational urgency, maintenance requirements, and flight schedules

• Support Aircraft on Ground (AOG) events through expedited&nbsp; logistics coordination and rapid fulfilment of critical material requirements

• Fulfil parts requisitions from internal stock or coordinate procurement, repair, and&nbsp; supplier activities to ensure on-time delivery

• Operate

At Flix, we offer a dynamic work environment with competitive pay, strong growth opportunities, and a tech-driven approach to making travel more accessible, sustainable, and affordable. &nbsp;

To strengthen our team in Portugal, we are looking for a motivated and driven Shop Employee (m/f/d) for our point of sale at the FlixBus Shop in Coimbra . You will support the day-to-day running of the shop, deliver high-quality service to our passengers, and help ensure smooth operations throughout your shift. This is a shift-based role, with shifts scheduled across the full week, including weekdays and weekends.&nbsp;

NB: Please submit your CV in English language!

About the Role

• Provide high-quality service to passengers, including assistance with boarding, transfers, travel disruptions such as delays, and clear travel information in Portuguese and English &nbsp;

• Manage ticket sales, provide after sale services, and daily cash handling in the Flix Shop &nbsp;

• Manage reservations, cancellations and adjust bookings in case of delays or changes, communicating with passengers and partners when needed, handle unexpected situations with minimal impact &nbsp;

• Support smooth station operations by coordinating with dispatchers and station teams during check-in and helping ensure correct luggage handling and passenger flow &nbsp;

• Assist drivers with mobile apps and ticket control, and help resolve issues to meet FlixBus quality and safety standards &nbsp;

• Inspect bus stops and surrounding infrastructure to ensure timetables, signage, and other elements meet FlixBus standards, coordinating updates or repairs when needed &nbsp;

About You

• Previous experience in customer service, transportation, logistics, or administration &nbsp;

• Proactive and self-motivated, taking ownership of tasks and working independently with minimal supervision &nbsp;

• Strong organizational skills and attention to detail, with the ability to manage multiple tasks in a dynamic environment &nbsp;

• Strong verbal and written communication skills &nbsp;

• Resilient and calm under pressure, able to stay focused and solution-oriented during busy periods and unexpected disruptions &nbsp;

• A strong team player who communicates openly, supports colleagues, and contributes to a positive shift atmosphere &nbsp;

• Comfortable with computers and digital tools &nbsp;

• Willing to work according to a shift schedule established with the team, which may include evenings, weekends, or early mornings &nbsp;

• Fluent in Portuguese and English ; other languages are a strong advantage &nbsp;

We recognize that everyone carries a unique set of valuable skills and experiences. If you think you could have an impact even though you don't meet 100% of the requirements, we still encourage you to apply. We want to hear from you! &nbsp;

NB: Please submit your CV in English language!

What We Offer

• Travel perks : 12 free Flix vouchers + 12 discount vouchers for friends &amp; family

• Wellbeing support : Access confidential 1:1 counselling, courses, and stress management for yourself and up to four family members

• Learning &amp; Development : Take advantage of language classes, training courses, and expert-led sessions to grow your skills

• Mentoring Program : Connect with experienced colleagues to gain insights and accelerate your career

• Other : Urban Sports Club discount , meal allowance , Lisbon Viva transportation discount

To view more local benefits specific to each office location, please check out this link:&nbsp; Locations - Flix Career

Why Join Flix?

At Flix, you’ll find teams that rally together to overcome challenges and spark creativity. We believe in ownership culture - giving you the freedom to take initiative, make an impact, and shape your own career path.
As we continue to expand across the globe, you can make a real difference in how we work.

If you’re ready to grow and lead your journey, Flix is the place for you!&nbsp;

